rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be recorded using the structured YAML
    decision schema instead of unstructured narrative text.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: ADR is the single source of truth for architectural decisions; all other
    representations must be derived from them to prevent inconsistencies.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Newly created patterns must be classified as supporting by default to ensure
    validation through evidence before being considered core.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers to maintain clear separation of concerns.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines the precedence model for resolving conflicts: Global Rules > Project
    Rules > Prompt Rules.'
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence to ensure grounding in observed behavior.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Aligns pattern maturity levels with governance decision statuses to prevent
    premature promotion of unvalidated patterns.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that signal promotion to patterns must satisfy recurrence, system
    impact, reusability, and stability criteria.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated artifacts like AEM and AID must summarize authoritative sources
    and must not own state or become authoritative themselves.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All runtime-native workflows must conform to the CAS Workflow Execution
    Model and its separation-of-concerns principles.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of architecture items must be derived from their decision
    status; items not 'accepted' cannot be marked 'DONE'.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects participate in a shared knowledge workspace and must not recreate
    global governance structures or templates.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source for planning state; generated
    artifacts must derive status from this registry.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures the Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) reflects and does not contradict
    decisions recorded in ADRs.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be system-proposed and explicitly accepted,
    rejected, or deferred by a human architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADRs before being
    reflected in AEM or other governance artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational primitives rather than specific
    implementations or strategies.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core must be supported by strong evidence, preferably
    from multiple sources or system runs.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the semantic contract for architecture terminology to ensure clarity
    between intent, state, and decision lifecycles.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
